# ✅ **Assignment 8 – Written Answers (Plaintext)**

**1. Are any of your predicted response values from your best model scientifically meaningless? Explain.**

Yes.
Because the model uses linear relationships, it can produce predictions that fall outside the biological range of mushroom growth. For example, some predicted values are close to zero or slightly negative when Light is low. Mushrooms cannot have negative growth rates, so any negative or unrealistic values produced by the model are scientifically meaningless. These values occur because the model extrapolates beyond the limits of the real dataset and does not “know” biological constraints.

---

**2. In your plots, did you find any non-linear relationships? Provide one resource that explains how to model non-linear relationships in R.**

Yes.
The scatterplots of **GrowthRate vs Light** and **GrowthRate vs Nitrogen** show curvature and non-linear patterns. Growth does not increase at a constant rate across these predictors. This suggests that a simple linear model cannot fully capture the biological responses, and a non-linear modeling approach (such as polynomial regression) would fit the data better.

A clear online resource explaining how to model non-linear (polynomial) relationships in R is:
[https://rpubs.com/rwilliams/69210](https://rpubs.com/rwilliams/69210)

